 \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/30/zig-ai-ban/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-30\",\n    \"topics\": [\"zig\", \"llms\", \"ai\", \"generative-ai\", \"open-source\"],\n    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Zig's 'Contributor Poker' Philosophy: Betting on People, Not PRs\",\n    \"description\": \"Loris Cro, Zig Software Foundation VP of Community, explains Zig's strict LLM ban as 'contributor poker' - you bet on the contributor, not the cards. The project values growing new contributors over landing perfect code. LLM assistance breaks this model because reviewing AI-written PRs doesn't help build trusted, long-term contributors.\",\n    \"author\": \"Loris Cro (via Simon Willison)\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/30/contributor-poker/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-30\",\n    \"topics\": [\"zig\", \"ai\", \"llms\", \"ai-ethics\", \"open-source\", \"ai-assisted-programming\"],\n    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Bun's 4x Performance Improvement Can't Be Upstreamed Due to Zig's AI Ban\",\n    \"description\": \"Bun achieved a 4x performance improvement after adding parallel semantic analysis to their Zig fork, but won't upstream it due to Zig's ban on LLM-authored contributions. Bun was acquired by Anthropic in December 2025 and makes heavy use of AI assistance.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/30/bun-zig-ai-ban/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-30\",\n    \"topics\": [\"zig\", \"bun\", \"anthropic\", \"javascript\", \"ai\", \"open-source\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"LLM 0.32a0: Major Backwards-Compatible Refactor Released\",\n    \"description\": \"Simon Willison released LLM 0.32a0, a major backwards-compatible refactor of his Python LLM library and CLI tool. The alpha includes consequential changes he's been working to